Chapter: WebSocket Vector Test
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Encode chapter WebSocket

 WebSocket against the values RFC 6455 prints in its own text: the
 worked accept-key example, the unmasked text frame, and the masked
 client frame beside it.

 The masked frame is asserted in both directions against the same
 published bytes. Encoding is required to produce them and decoding
 is required to recover the payload from them, so neither direction
 is being checked against the other -- a codec that agreed only with
 itself would satisfy a round trip and fail both of these.

 The unmasked encode line is the control. It passed before any of
 this chapter was corrected and it must keep passing, which is what
 distinguishes a real repair from a probe that never worked.

Section: Helpers

  dec-list : List Integer -> Text
  dec-list (bs) = dl bs 0 (list-length bs) ""

  dl : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  dl (bs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let sep = if i == 0 then "" else " "
    in dl bs (i + 1) n (acc & sep & show (list-at bs i))

  payload-of : List Integer -> List Integer
  payload-of (bs) = (ws-decode-frame bs).ws-payload

  count-cr : List Integer -> Integer
  count-cr (bs) = cc bs 0 0

  cc : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  cc (bs) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length bs then acc
    else cc bs (i + 1) (if list-at bs i == 13 then acc + 1 else acc)

Section: Vector

  client-key : Text = "dGhlIHNhbXBsZSBub25jZQ=="

  masked-hello : List Integer = [129, 133, 55, 250, 33, 61, 127, 159, 77, 81, 88]

  mask-key : List Integer = [55, 250, 33, 61]

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("accept=" & ws-accept-key client-key)
    print-line-uni ("encode=" & dec-list (ws-encode-text "Hello"))
    print-line-uni ("decoded=" & dec-list (payload-of masked-hello))
    print-line-uni ("masked=" & dec-list (ws-encode-text-masked "Hello" mask-key))
    print-line-uni ("hs-cr=" & show (count-cr (ws-handshake-response-bytes client-key)))
  end

